  <content>
    <section>
      <para>A marine biologist estimates that a structure of coral has a volume of 1,200 cubic centimeters and that its volume
  doubles each year.</para>
      <para>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_08_03_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Write an equation of the form \(y=a\cdot b^t\) representing the relationship, where \(t\) is time in
        years since the coral was measured and \(y\) is volume of coral in cubic centimeters. (You need to figure
        out what numbers \(a\) and \(b\) are in this situation.)</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
   </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>\(y=1,200\cdot 2^t\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
        <item>Find the volume of the coral when \(t\) is 5, 1, 0, –1, and –2. Note that when \(t = -1\), this
    represents one year before the marine biologist made the original estimate.
 </item>
      </list>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>Time (years)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>1</entry>
            <entry>0</entry>
            <entry>-1</entry>
            <entry>-2</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>Volume of Coral (cubic centimeters)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>a.____
      </entry>
            <entry>b.____
      </entry>
            <entry>c.____
      </entry>
            <entry>d.____
      </entry>
            <entry>e.____
      </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_58888de2-7d9b-405d-a5bb-e1757fd262c3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Enter the volume of coral when t = 5. Do not enter commas in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 3800 cubic centimeters</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 3800 cubic centimeters</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_48eecec1-7ae0-48d7-8d2d-912f221f88f8" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Enter the volume of coral when t = 1. Do not enter commas in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 2400 cubic centimeters</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 2400 cubic centimeters</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ec7943f4-d9f7-430c-86f7-b965ddc0b967" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Enter the volume of coral when t = 0. Do not enter commas in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 1200 cubic centimeters</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 1200 cubic centimeters</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d325a246-3666-4e89-87ff-f46f511a3cb8" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Enter the volume of coral when t = -1. Do not enter commas in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 600 cubic centimeters</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 600 cubic centimeters</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_839cb86e-da3a-45fc-9279-ca3b5bc704a5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            
            <para>Enter the volume of coral when t = -2. Do not enter commas in your answer.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 300 cubic centimeters</para>
            <para>Nice try! The correct answer is 300 cubic centimeters</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What does it mean, in this situation, when \(t\) is –2?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>This represents the time 2 years before the scientist made the estimate of 1,200 cubic centimeters.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>In a certain year, the volume of the coral is 37.5 cubic centimeters. Which year is this? Be prepared to show
        your reasoning.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(t\) is –5, or 5 years before the scientist made the estimate of 1,200 cubic centimeters.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
    <note class="self-check">
      (    <para>Using the equation \(p=10,000\cdot 2^d\), find the value of \(p\) when \(d = -2\).</para>)
        </note>

        <section>
          <title>Additional Resources</title>
          
  <section><title>Interpreting Negative Exponents in Exponential Growth</title><para>Let’s look at a problem involving an exponential growth equation and negative exponents.</para>
    <para>A forest fire has been burning for several days. The burned area, in acres, is given by the equation \(y=4800\cdot
      2^d\), where \(d\) is the number of days since the area of the fire was first measured.</para>
      <para>
        1. Let’s complete the table.
      </para>
      
      <table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
        <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>\(d\), days since first measurement</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Process column</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>\(y\), acres burned since fire started</emphasis></entry></row>
        <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>\(= 4800 \cdot 2^0 = 4800 \cdot 1 \)
            </entry>
            <entry>4800</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              \(= 4800 \cdot 2^1 = 4800 \cdot \frac12 \)
            </entry>
            <entry>2400</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>–2
            </entry>
            <entry>0
            </entry>
            <entry>c. _____</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>d. _____</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>–5
            </entry>
    
            <entry>0
            </entry><entry>e. _____</entry>
            
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
      <para>To determine the value of \(y\), given \(d\), follow these steps:</para>
      <para><emphasis>Example 1</emphasis></para>
      <para>Determine the value for \(y\) when \(d = -2\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> -Substitute the given domain value for d into the expression.</para>
      <para>\(4800 \cdot 2^{-2}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> -Evaluate the exponential value. Recall that a negative exponent represents how many times
        the reciprocal of the base should be multiplied.</para>
      <para>\(= 4800 \cdot (\frac{1}{2})^2 = 4800 \cdot \frac14\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> -Evaluate the remaining expression to determine \(y\).</para>
      <para>\(= 1200\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Example 2</emphasis></para>
      <para>Determine the value for \(y\) when \(d = -3\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> -Substitute the given domain value for d into the expression.</para>
      <para>\(4800 \cdot 2^{-3}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> -Evaluate the exponential value. Recall that a negative exponent represents how many times
        the reciprocal of the base should be multiplied.</para>
      <para>\(= 4800 \cdot (\frac{1}{2})^3 = 4800 \cdot \frac18\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> -Evaluate the remaining expression to determine \(y\).</para>
      <para>\(= 600\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Example 3</emphasis></para>
      <para>Determine the value for \(y\) when \(d = -5\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> -Substitute the given domain value for d into the expression.</para>
      <para>\(4800 \cdot 2^{-5}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> -Evaluate the exponential value. Recall that a negative exponent represents how many times
        the reciprocal of the base should be multiplied.</para>
      <para>\(= 4800 \cdot (\frac{1}{2})^5 = 4800 \cdot \frac{1}{32}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> -Evaluate the remaining expression to determine \(y\).</para>
      <para>\(= 150\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Example 4</emphasis></para>
      <para>What does the value of \(y\) tell you about the area burned in the fire when \(d=-1\)?</para>
      <para>The \(y\) value at \(d= -1\) represents the fact that 2,400 acres had burned 1 day before the first measurement was
        taken.</para>
        <para><emphasis>Example 5</emphasis></para>
        <para>How much area had the fire burned a week before it measured 4,800 acres? Explain your reasoning.</para>
      <para>Since there are 7 days in a week, to find the area burned a week before the fire was measured, we need to determine
        the value of \(y\) when \(d = -7\).</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> -Substitute the given domain value for d into the expression.</para>
      <para>\(4800 \cdot 2^{-7}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> -Evaluate the exponential value. Recall that a negative exponent represents how many times
        the reciprocal of the base should be multiplied.</para>
      <para>\(= 4800 \cdot \frac12 ^7 = 4800 \cdot \frac{1}{128}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> -Evaluate the remaining expression to determine \(y\).</para>
      <para>\(= 37.5\)</para>
      <para>\(37.5\) acres had burned a week before the fire measured \(4,800\) acres. The value is found by substituting
        \(-7\) for d since that represents \(7\) days before the first measurement of \(4,800\) acres.</para>
    </list>
    <exercise>
      <problem>
        
        <para>The value of a home in 2015 was $400,000. Its value has doubled each decade.</para>
        
        <para>
            If \(v\) is the value of the home, in dollars, write an equation for \(v\) in terms of \(d\), the number of
            decades since 2015.
         </para>
        <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
       </para>
      
      </problem><solution>
      <para>Compare your answers:</para>
      
      <para>\(v=400,000\cdot 2^d\)</para>
    
    </solution></exercise>

    <note class="try"><title>Try It: Interpreting Negative Exponents in Exponential Growth</title><exercise id="_2b67ffaa-723e-487c-8c95-d16dc41948b7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is \(v\) when \(d=-1\)?
           </para>
          </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(v=200,000\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-1}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-1}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac12\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac12\)
            \(v=200,000\)
          \(v=200,000\)
         </para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: \(v=200,000\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-1}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-1}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac12\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac12\)
            \(v=200,000\)
          \(v=200,000\)
         </para></solution></exercise>
         
         <exercise>
      <problem>
        
        <para>What does this value mean?</para>
        <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
       </para>
      
      </problem><solution>
      <para>Compare your answers:</para>
      
      <para>This means the home had a value of 50,000 in 1985, three decades before 2015.</para>
    
    </solution></exercise>
    <exercise>
      <problem>
        
        <para>What does this value mean?</para>
        <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
       </para>
      
      </problem><solution>
      <para>Compare your answers:</para>
      
      <para>This means the home had a value of 200,000 in 2005, one decade before 2015.</para>
    </solution></exercise>
<exercise id="_008191ca-6f8e-4a92-9d5d-a47673938ec1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is \(v\) when \(d=-3\)?</para>
          </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(v=50,000\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-3}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-3}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac18\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac18\)
            \(v=50,000\)
          \(v=50,000\)
         </para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is: \(v=50,000\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-3}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot 2^{-3}\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac18\)
            \(v=400,000\cdot\frac18\)
            \(v=50,000\)
          \(v=50,000\)
         </para></solution></exercise></note>
    </section>
        </section>
      </section>
